<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A = {\{2, 8\}}</m>, <m>B = {\{2, 8, 10\}}</m>, <m>C = {\{1, 5\}}</m> and <m>D = {\{x : x \text{ is a whole number}, x + 5 = 5\}}</m>. Is each statement true or false?</p><p>(a) <m>A \subset B</m> [ True | False ]  </p><p>(b) <m>B \supseteq C</m> [ True | False ]  </p><p>(c) <m>A</m> and <m>C</m> are disjoint. [ True | False ]  </p><p>(d) <m>D</m> is a singleton. [ True | False ]  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) <m>A \subset B</m> needs every element of <m>A</m> to be in <m>B</m>, and <m>A \neq B</m>; here every element of <m>A</m> is in <m>B</m> and <m>A \neq B</m>, so <m>A \subset B</m> is true.</p><p>(b) <m>B \supseteq C</m> means every element of <m>C</m> is in <m>B</m>; here <m>1</m> and <m>5</m> are not in <m>B</m>, so the statement is false.</p><p>(c) <m>A \cap C = \{\,\}</m>, so <m>A</m> and <m>C</m> have no element in common: they are disjoint.</p><p>(d) <m>D = \{0\}</m> has <m>1</m> element; a singleton has exactly one element, so the statement is true.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>True</p></answer>
    <answer><p>False</p></answer>
    <answer><p>True</p></answer>
    <answer><p>True</p></answer>
</stack-static>